Z||000000||aubicon||08-07-2001||12:28 AM||||when you turn the ignition on and let the fuel pump run for its 2 second deration the fuel pressure goes to 42 psi(factory spects 40.5 - 47 psi). then when you start the motor the pressure drops to about 34 psi, if i rev the motor it will jump back up to the low 40's, then drop back to 34 psi when the engine returns to idle. i have a feeling that it is the fuel pressure regulator. what do you think? any idias or reasurances would be greatly appritiated.||||reg||3
Z||000001||87GTZ34||08-07-2001||10:48 AM||||That is normal operation.  The reg is 'directed' by manifold vacuum.  High vacuum (idle) lowers the fuel pressure and low vacuum (WOT) raises the fuel pressure.  Does this make sense to you? Higher RPM more fuel, lower RPM less fuel.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||aubicon||08-07-2001||10:07 PM||||the fuel pressure change at different rpm's i understand, but at idle the pressure is only at 34 psi that is below spects, is this correct or do i have something wrong in the fuel system?||||reg||1
